'''andromonœcious''' (an″drọ̄-mọ̄-nē′shius), ''a.'' [< Gr. ἀνήρ (ἀνδρ-), male, + ''monœcious'', q. v.] In ''bot.'', having hermaphrodite and male flowers upon the same plant, but with no female flowers. ''Darwin.''
